[gd_scene load_steps=3 format=3]

; Riftwrought — ROGUELITE I2: PLAYABLE THREE-LANE LEVEL-UP CHOICE REVIEW V1 (decision D-293).
;
; One question, asked in play: collect real Experience Motes to exactly the Level 1
; requirement -> a three-card panel opens on its own and holds the world still ->
; exactly one lane is chosen -> the run is at Level 2 with that choice recorded in
; the expedition's temporary build, and play resumes. The chosen effects are NOT
; applied to the character in this review.
;
; IT IS NOT THE PROJECT ENTRYPOINT AND MUST NEVER BECOME ONE. `run/main_scene` is
; still the Prototype App. Launch this scene with Run Current Scene, never Run
; Project, or:
;   godot --path game res://scenes/roguelite/roguelite_level_up_choice_review.tscn -- --seed 99
;
; IT INHERITS THE ACCEPTED EXPERIENCE COLLECTION REVIEW SCENE (H9) AND ADDS NO NODE
; OF ITS OWN. The one line below this header that differs from that scene is the
; root's script, which EXTENDS H9's runtime: the accepted loop, its five
; Graveblades, the Experience Mote runtime, the markers and the review panel all
; come from the accepted scene and code, neither copied nor edited. The level-up
; panel and the temporary-build receipt are made in code at run time.
;
; Controls are the accepted core loop's, unchanged. Review keys are PHYSICAL:
;   F8 automatic mote pickup ON/OFF · F6 grid · [ ] camera distance · \ reset
;   F5 abandon the run
; While the level-up panel is open only the card controls answer: arrows / D-pad
; move between cards, Enter / (A) or a left click chooses. There is no close.

